window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["vw/scirocco-13"]={"scirocco-13-activate-bluetooth-on-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth on the RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION: Not all RNS-315 are equipped with a Bluetooth module.</strong> </p>\n<figure><table><thead><tr><td>Module compatibility list</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3C0 035 279</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 A</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 B</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 C</td><td>Yes (conditional)</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 D</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 E</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 F</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 G</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 H</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 J</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 K</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>You can also remove the RNS 315 from its slot to check. Behind it, you’ll find a label with the RNS-315’s MAC address.<br/>If the MAC address contains only zeros (MAC: 00:00:00:00:00:00), your RNS-315 is not equipped with the Bluetooth module. </p>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns_315_j_mac_non-6328b9e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns315_mac_oui-eed1a386.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>3</strong><br/>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Uncheck the “Telephone Transceiver inactive” box</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS315_3C0-035-279_Module37_Byte3-74e93c9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-activate-coming-leaving-home":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Activates Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 <em>(AFTER the end of 2009)</em>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>12</strong>:<br/>Disable bit <strong>2</strong></p>\n<p>Byte <strong>17</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) active”<br/>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Check “Leaving-Home (CH) active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Line 1 <em>(BEFORE the end of 2009</em>):</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>23</strong>:<br/>Disable bit <strong>5</strong></p>","scirocco-13-activate-daytime-running-lights-drl-only-with-headlight-switch-in-auto-position":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate daytime running lights (DRL) only when the light <strong>switch</strong> is in Auto position.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>26</strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light (DRL) only active with Assistance Driving Light (ADL) active”.  </p>","scirocco-13-activate-hidden-menu-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the hidden menu in RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Developer mode (temporary)</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong><em>Enabled</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart RNS 315.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-035-279_Module37_Adaptation_Developer_mode_tem-59109da4.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-activate-hidden-menu-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the hidden menu in RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>56 – Radio</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 50</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1T0-035-680-C_Module37_Adaptation_Channel50-1a7d6a90.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-activate-off-road-mode-on-discover-pq":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add Offroad mode to Discover PQ with navigation.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 3 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_List_BAP_Gen2-compass_0x15</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass_over-threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Restart the Discover Media PQ (hold down the ON/OFF button for at least 5 seconds).</p>\n<p>Depending on your hardware and firmware, the off-road menu may appear directly in the Menu, or it may be hidden:<br/>Press the VOICE-MENU-NAV buttons to access the secret menu, where you’ll now find the OFFROAD screen:  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadpq-1024x768-39023fd7.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadmenupq-1024x619-dc3e8b4c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroad-1024x631-441bee99.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-activate-rearview-camera-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rearview camera after it has been installed on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510 or Discover MIB2 PQ (retrofit). <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h4>RCD/RNS :</h4>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>3</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>6</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) installed/active.”</p>\n<hr/>\n<h4>Discover MIB2 PQ:</h4>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte <strong>19</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>4</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) Low installed (PR-KA1).”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/C25A41FA-66F7-4FC9-B7F4-1761395A1D01-1024x483-11bbd3cf.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong><strong><strong>Line 2 (Optional, if parking assist is available)</strong> <strong>:</strong></strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>0</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>5</strong> to “Rear View Camera installed.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/CA86A611-2F74-4201-B791-7A74BC107A01-1024x482-c9f00e16.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><strong>Hardware upgrade :</strong></p>\n<p>The camera’s video cable is connected to the infotainment control unit. It is installed in the glovebox.   <br/><br/>The two pins from the backup camera are used in the 12-pin Quadlock connector (blue).<br/><br/>Quadblock Assignment :<br/><br/>Pin 6 = video line<br/>Pin 12 = shielding</p>","scirocco-13-activate-rns-510-voice-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate voice control on the RNS 510 (SDS).  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:</strong> RNS 510 firmware must be version v2660.</p>\n<p>Activating voice control brings up the “Voice control” menu in the RNS 510’s SETUP menu.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>3</strong>, check the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Microphone Diagnostics active</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>7</strong>, uncheck the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Voice Control inactive</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS510_Menu_Commande_Vocale-bf5955d7.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>To install the microphone, connect the microphone lead to the rear of the RNS 510. Connect to pins (Mic-)C1 and (Mic+)C7. </p>","scirocco-13-activate-the-discover-hidden-menu":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates the green hidden menu (green menu, hidden menu, testmode, engineer mode) on Discover MIB2.  </p>\n<p>/!\\ Caution: Making certain changes in the hidden menu may cause MIB2 to freeze or no longer start /!\\  </p>\n<p><em>For model Facelift (radio screen like Golf 7).  </em><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“S12345</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Developer mode</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value<strong>“activated</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Restart MIB2, keep MENU button pressed until testmode menu appears</em><br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode-bfa51f40.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode2-1024x576-7a0c833c.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-activate-turn-signals-in-us-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate US indicators. (Scirocco phase 1 only)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>Byte 7</strong>: Set value<strong> 32</strong> in <strong>Dec</strong> box (value in % of intensity, origin: 0)</p>\n<p>Decimal examples shown in yellow in the image:<br/>14 (corresponds to a 20% variation in the indicator lights)<br/>1E (corresponds to a 30% variation in the indicator lights)<br/>28 (corresponds to a 40% variation in the indicator lights)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-937-049-Q_Module09_Byte7-16502f21.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-adapting-brake-assist":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to configure brake assist.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>09</strong> (Brake Assist from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value</em><br/> 0<em>“medium” </em><br/>1 “low” (with low assistance, the brake pedal will be harder and more pressure will be required to brake)<br/>2 “high” (with high assistance, the brake pedal will be softer and less pressure will be required to brake)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/assistfreing6-05b83882.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-add-daytime-running-lights-drl-to-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to enable or disable daytime running lights (DRL) in the ODB (MFA). (2011+)</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>15</strong>: Bit <strong>7</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light (DRL) Active Adaptation (MFA+)”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlmfag6-54cdc95d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlmfag62-c1d9cfb9.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-add-mirror-adjustment-in-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add the mirror adjustment menu, synchronize or individual in the ODB (MFA). (2011+)</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>08</strong>: <em>Check Bit <strong>6</strong> </em><em>“Synchronized Mirror Adjustment</em>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mirrorg6-b05eff1b.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mirrorg62-c24fc65a.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/mirrorg63-c1fe0276.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-adjusting-light-sensor-sensitivity":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Adjusts the sensitivity of the light sensor.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>:  </em><br/><em>Bits <strong>3–4</strong>: Select from the drop-down list<br/>– 00 Normal light activation threshold<br/>– 08 Earlier light activation threshold (+20%)<br/>– 10 Light Activation Threshold earlier (+40%)<br/>– 08 Light Activation Threshold earlier (+60%)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Or if model less recent :</strong></p>\n<p>Byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/><strong>Bit 0-7</strong>: Light Sensor Correction</p>","scirocco-13-adjusting-the-volume-of-the-reversing-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust the volume of the reversing beep.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“10-Station assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select Channel: <em>“rear warning buzzer volume”. </em> </p>\n<p>Adjust value accordingly<br/>(default: 5)</p>","scirocco-13-ambient-lighting-intensity":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Used to adjust ambient lighting intensity.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>” then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 05</strong> (Footwell Lightning Dimming)  </p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select intensity from 20 to 100% (in 1% increments)</p>","scirocco-13-automatic-closing-of-windows-and-roof-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Automatically closes the windows and sunroof when it rains. </p>\n<p>The vehicle must be locked using the remote control for this to work. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf561-c90da3e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “2” and click ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf56-9439cbb9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte <strong>0</strong> and check bit <strong>2</strong> “<strong>Rain Closing active</strong>” to activate window and roof closing when it rains:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-5-d61c5dd9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>7 – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu</p>\n<p> Then click “OK”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-7-353fb01b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 <em>(AFTER the end of 2009)</em></strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select <em>Byte<strong> 4</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “Comfort Operation Windows/Sunroof via Rain Sensor (0 = nonrecurring / 1 = permanent)” </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6: </strong> Check “Comfort Operation Windows/Sunroof via Rain Sensor (Rain Closing) active” </em> </p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 <em>(BEFORE the end of 2009) </em></strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>46 – Central Conv</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “<strong> Long Coding Helper</strong>”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>9</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Closing (0 = nonrecurring / 1 = permanent)” </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Uncheck “Comfort Closing via Rain Light Sensor (Rain Closing) inactive” </em> </p>","scirocco-13-automatic-door-locks":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set automatic door locking from 15km/h.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 <em>(AFTER the end of 2009)</em>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong><strong><em>09 – Cent. Elect.</em></strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2 : </strong> Check “Auto-Lock active”. </em> </p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1 </strong><em><strong><em>(BEFORE the end of 2009)</em></strong></em><br/><br/><strong> </strong> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4<strong>– </strong>Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres_vw-auto-loc-ce03b1da.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 <em>(if the adaptation channel is not activated)</em>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Auto-Lock (automatic locking from 15 km/h)”. </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-automatic-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set automatic door unlocking when the ignition key is removed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 <em>(AFTER the end of 2009)</em>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong><strong><em>09 – Cent. Elect.</em></strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0 : </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Auto-Unlock active”. </em> </p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1 <em>(BEFORE the end of 2009)</em></strong><em>: </em><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 05</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw-door-unlock-798a1163.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 <em>(if the adaptation channel is not activated) :</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Auto-Unlock (unlocking after removing key from ignition)”. </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-automatic-headlight-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte 0 Bit 0: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-automatic-headlight-activation-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte 0 Bit 1: Check “Rain Light Function Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-automatically-folding-mirrors":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically folds mirrors when vehicle is locked.  </p>\n<p>For 4th generation door modules (models from 2013) activation is possible with VCDS VAG-COM (Procedure with VCP for 3rd generation at bottom of page).</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>42 – Driver’s door</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“04354</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select the Channel:<strong>“System_Parameter_0-System</strong> Parameter Byte8” in the drop-down list.<br/><br/>Replace the Value <strong>90</strong> (if several values the 90 is in the middle, example: xxxx90xxxx )</p>\n<p>Set value according to mirror opening mode: <br/> – <strong>95</strong> (mirrors<em> will deploy when door is opened)</em><br/><em> – <strong>99</strong> (mirrors will deploy when ignition is switched on)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/DCA8744A-30AB-4C05-B633-4F3B76D90C50-4f152256.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>VCP</strong> (Vag Can Pro) : For 3rd generation door modules (models up to 2011) activation is only possible with VCP.</p>\n<p>Click on Guided Functions then select the “Convenience” module on the right then “Activation automatic folder mirrors in UDS door control units (Passat/ Tiguan / Jetta)”.</p>\n<p>Setting, Command: “Folding with driver door” or “Folding with ignition” = with driver door or with key</p>\n<p>Engine/Car type : CAN TP20 1K0/5K0</p>\n<p>Start the procedure, but don’t forget to save the Conductor 42 door module with access code 04354.</p>","scirocco-13-change-discover-start-logo":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to display another logo at launch, and a color to match the finish of your Discover PQ.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte<strong>“18</strong>”<br/>Then modify the hexadecimal value of the box in<strong>“3)</strong>” of the long code:<br/><br/>00 – Default<br/>01 – Hybride<br/>02 – GTD<br/>03 – GTI (red color)<br/>04 – Blue Motion<br/>05 – E- (electric)<br/>06 – R-Line<br/>07 – R (blue color)<br/>08 – Alltrack<br/>09 – GTE</p>\n<p>If you have a bit 0-7 drop-down list, select your vehicle or modify the byte directly with the list. If your bits are hidden, modify in the binary value : </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/bits-logo-discover-be1ebdf0.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_discover_pro_look_carbon_byte18_MMI-Audi-A3-MQB-677483cb.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/hqdefault-856d3e0d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/maxresdefaulet-1024x576-1-9caa5322.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/maxresdefault-1024x768-1-76be041f.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-change-the-theme-of-rcd-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the display theme of the RCD 510 and RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” for RNS510 and “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” for RCD510.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>4-5</strong>: Select from 3 themes</em><br/><em>“00 Display Variant: Highline</em><br/><em>“10 Display Variant: Sportsline</em><br/><em>“20 Display Variant: Premium</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/69C76009-6EC7-465A-A676-8E39BA840A6B-6689b9e0.webp\"/><figcaption>Highline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3A58F148-9FBB-4DD8-BF05-E03A5351E3A8-e9b6cb9b.webp\"/><figcaption>Sportsline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4894A3B7-2ED2-4A75-9D46-CA3BFCF5A76C-8fb8de15.webp\"/><figcaption>Premium</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD / RNS 510 must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","scirocco-13-changing-the-image-of-the-rcd-rns-ops":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the vehicle image of the OPS (parking aid) on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Encoding 07</strong>,” then ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose Byte<strong> 6</strong> or <strong>9</strong></p>\n<p><em>Select the vehicle from the drop-down menu:</em><br/><br/>00 = via CAN<br/>01 = Polo 6R<br/>02 = New Beetle<br/>03 = New Beetle Cabrio<br/>04 = Scirocco<br/>05 = Golf 5<br/>06 = Jetta<br/>07 = Golf 6 Variant<br/>08 = Golf 6 Cabrio<br/>09 = Touran<br/>0A = Golf Plus<br/>0C = Tiguan<br/>0D = Sharan<br/>0E = EOS<br/>0F = Passat 3C<br/>10 = Passat Limousine<br/>11 = Passat Variant<br/>13 = Caddy<br/>14 = T5<br/>2C = Skoda Octavia<br/>2D = Skoda Octavia Kombi<br/>2E = Skoda Superb Kombi</p>\n<p><br/>For the aftermarket <strong>RCD 330</strong> (original Passat or Jetta image) for the Scirocco image: <br/>Byte <strong>6</strong><br/>Uncheck all boxes (normally only bit 0 and bit 2 are checked)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_0863-9500c82e.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_0864-978ed9ed.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD or RNS must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","scirocco-13-comfort-turn-signal":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Comfort Turn Signal</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – Choose between “<strong>1</strong>” and “<strong>5</strong>,” then confirm.</p>","scirocco-13-coming-leaving-home-with-fog-lamps":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables fog lamps to be used for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>17</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-coming-leaving-home-with-the-xenons":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Activates xenon headlamps instead of fog lamps for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>17</strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-coming-home-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is locked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01</strong> (Coming-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>","scirocco-13-corner-lights-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate cornering lights with fog lamps.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1, For models up to end 2009:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible for vehicles with a 30 Byte power plant.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>23</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Internal Turn Light Control Algorithm active”.</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3-4</strong>: Select “08 Turn Lights via fog lights” from the drop-down list</em></p>\n<p><em>Or disable bit <strong>3</strong> and <strong>4</strong></em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Line 2, For models after end 2009:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4-Activation-des-feux-en-virage-sur-Golf-5-et-6-f4e51c90.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select  </p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Cornering Light Activation Time limited”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Check “Cornering Lights via Front Fog Lights activ</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-255e876b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – After this operation, click on the “Output” menu<br/>Then validate “OK”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-2a08cc40.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-corner-lights-in-reverse":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to activate the cornering lights with the fog lamps when reversing.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>26</strong>: Bit <strong>6</strong>: Check “Enabling Cornering Light with Reverse Gear active”.</p>","scirocco-13-cruise-control-activation-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to activate GRA cruise control (retrofit). </p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible after retrofitting cruise control switch and <a href=\"https://wiki.ross-tech.com/wiki/index.php/Steering_Wheel_Control_Module_Versions\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">check that your multifunction steering wheel is compatible (midline or highline)</a>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>01 – Motor</strong> “.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on ” <strong>Coding II (11) or Login 11</strong> “. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur1-1c279499.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Then enter code <strong>11463</strong>, then <strong>OK</strong> (Do It!)</p>\n<p>The code 11463 is used to <strong>activate</strong> the controller, to <strong>deactivate</strong> it if necessary the code is 16167.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur2-6871f13e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>16 – Multifunction handwheel</strong> “.<br/><br/>4<strong>– </strong>Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong> “. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur3-945b80f3.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Options: We note in the penultimate section (0xxxx<strong>?</strong>x):<br/><br/>0 = No regulator installed (CCS not installed)<br/>1 = Regulator installed with 6 positions on a separate switch (CCS with 6 positions …. etc)<br/>3 = Regulator installed with 4 positions on the blinker switch (CCS with 4 positions via Blinker Stalk)</p>\n<p>So replace the “<strong>?</strong>” with the 3 for commodo regulator.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”, then click on ” Select</strong> “. <strong><strong>01 – Engine</strong></strong> ” .<br/><br/>4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select byte<strong>“5</strong>“<br/>Check bit<strong>“5</strong>” Cruise Control System (CCS) installed</p>\n<p>Or byte <strong>6</strong> bit <strong>0</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur5-1024x491-af7739d1.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-daytime-running-lights-deactivation-drl-with-handbrake-on":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) when the handbrake is engaged. (After the end of 2009)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: If this is a hidden bit, replace the last <strong>0</strong> on the right side of the binary number with <strong>a 1</strong>. (<strong>10001000</strong> =&gt; <strong>10001001</strong>)</em></p>","scirocco-13-deactivate-brake-pad-warning-light":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to disable the brake pad wear warning light on the OBD (On-Board Diagnostics) system, for example, for brake pads without a sensor or if the sensor is malfunctioning / Brake Pad Warning Light Deactivation. </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong><strong>Line 1 ( For models before 2010 ! )</strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>17 – Instruments</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on <strong>“Coding –</strong> 07”  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> <em>–  <em>The third and fourth digits of the code (xx<strong>??</strong>x0x) are used to change the settings for the Instrument module. To turn off the brake pad warning light, subtract <strong>01</strong> from these digits. </em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instruments-Coding-Golf5-2c5d8d07.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In the example above, the initial code is: <strong>0027103</strong></p>\n<p>To turn off the brake pad warning light, simply recode it as follows: <strong>0026103 </strong><em>(27 – 01 = 26)</em></p>\n<p>To turn on the brake pad warning light: +01</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong><strong><strong>Line 2 ( For models after 2010 ! )</strong></strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>17 – Instruments</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Cliquer sur « <strong>Codage – 07</strong> » puis cliquer sur « <strong>Assistant Codage Long</strong>« .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>: “<br/>” Then uncheck bit <strong>0: </strong> <strong>“Brakepad warning active/installed”</strong> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant-frein-d4619ec9.gif\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-deactivate-mirrorlink":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable or remove MirrorLink from App-Connect on the MIB Discover PQ. The MirrorLink service has not been natively available on Android since June 1, 2020. For a direct connection to Android Auto.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicle configuration-Mirror_link</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Disabled</strong>” and confirm.</p>","scirocco-13-deactivate-rear-wiper-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate automatic activation of the rear wiper.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>:<br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on <strong>“Long Coding Helper”</strong>:</p>\n<p><em>Byte 1 :</em><br/><em>Bit 7: Uncheck “Rear Wiper with Front Wiper continiously active”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Byte 2 : </em><br/><em>Bit 0: Uncheck “Rear Wiper with Front Wiper intermitent active”.</em></p>","scirocco-13-deactivate-windshield-washer-indicator":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong><strong>Line 1 ( For models before 2010 ! )</strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> <em>–  <em>The third and fourth coding digits (xx<strong>??</strong>x0x) are used to modify Instrument module options. To remove the ice-washer indicator, subtract <strong>04</strong> from these digits. </em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instruments-Coding-Golf5-2c5d8d07.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In the example above, the initial coding is: <strong>0027103</strong></p>\n<p>To remove the windscreen washer indicator, simply recode as follows: <strong>0023103 </strong><em>(27 – 04 = 23)</em></p>\n<p>To activate the ice washer indicator: +04</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong><strong>Line 2 ( For models after 2010 ! )</strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>2: </strong>“<strong>Washer Fluid warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglace-edc83d4f.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-defrost-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the operating time for mirror and rear window defrosting.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong> (Rear Window &amp; Outside Mirror Heater Activation Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>1 to 254 min</strong> (in 1 min increments).</p>","scirocco-13-delete-alarm-belt":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 ( For models before 2010! )</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>” . 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> –  <em>The third and fourth coding digits (xx<strong>??</strong>x0x) are used to modify Instrument module options. To suppress the belt alarm, subtract <strong>2</strong> from these digits. </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instruments-Coding-Golf5-2c5d8d07.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In the example above, the initial coding (with belt alarm) is: <strong>0023103</strong></p>\n<p>To delete the belt alarm, simply recode as follows: <strong>0021103 </strong><em>(23 – 02 = 21)</em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Line 2 ( For models after 2010 ! )</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>1</strong>” <br/>Then uncheck Bit “<strong>1</strong>”: “<strong>Seatbelt warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-disable-am-frequency-on-discover":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the AM radio frequency on the Discover PQ (the AM radio frequency is rarely used, unlike the FM radio frequency). <br/><em><em>For Scirocco Facelift (Mib2 screen like Golf 7). </em></em> </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>14</strong></p>\n<p>Set bit <strong>1</strong> <strong>“AM_disable</strong></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>","scirocco-13-deactivating-fog-lamps-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to disable/enable the fog lights for a retrofit installation of an R-series front bumper without a bulb error. (To enable them, check the bits.)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1</strong><em><strong> (AFTER late 2009)</strong> </em>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Code 07</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte <strong>14: </strong> </em><br/>Uncheck <em>Bit <strong>0</strong> ” </em> <em>Fog Lights Installed</em> “</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/image-43511819.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1 <em>(BEFORE the end of 2009)</em></strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Code 07</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte <strong>0: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Uncheck “Fog Lights Installed”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/scandinavie_194-c7df4fa8.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-disable-plate-light-control-odb-led-error":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Disables license plate light control. Useful when installing LED bulbs without resistance or for error prevention.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Bytes <strong>23</strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Uncheck: “Lamp Monitoring (Cold) License Plate Lamps Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/led_plaque5-odt_147-d36567c5.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-door-lighting-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables door lighting to be activated after retrofitting.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>42 – Driver’s door</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Add <strong>64</strong> to the existing coding.</em></p>\n<p>Repeat for <strong>“52 – Passenger door”</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Connection :  </strong></p>\n<p>The cables must be connected to the 32-pin B connector on the door.</p>\n<p>Pin 18 → Red [+12V]<br/>Pin 19 → Brown [- Ground]</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw-golf-scirocco-door-electronics-module-9f4c48e6.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/door-lights-retfofit-coding-vw-scirocco-golf-6-1392861d.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-door-lock-confirmation-key":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: To set the door lock confirmation when the key is used (for Scirocco before end 2009).   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 11</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: </strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Tick “Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks” (confirmation with beep/horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/locking_196-096e4b1a.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-door-lock-confirmation-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the door lock confirmation when using the remote control. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1<em> (AFTER the end of 2009)</em>:</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong> Select Byte <strong>5</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation via Horn Enabled”</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>10</strong> – (Unlock sound)<em>: </em><br/><em>Set value to<strong> 1</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>7 –</strong> Select Channel <strong>11</strong> – (Tone on lock):<br/><em>Set value to<strong> 1</strong></em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1 <strong><em>(BEFORE the end of 2009)</em></strong> </strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 10</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vagcom-golf5-e5c80be6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 </strong><em><strong>(If the adaptation channel is not activated</strong>)</em> <strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Tick “Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control” (confirmation with Beep/Horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/locking_196-096e4b1a.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-door-unlock-confirmation-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to set the door unlock confirmation when using the remote control.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1<em> (AFTER the end of 2009)</em>:</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong> Select Byte <strong>5</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>4: </strong> Check “Unlocking Confirmation via Horn active” </p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>10</strong> – (Unlock sound)<em>: </em><br/><em>Set value to<strong> 1</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>7 –</strong> Select Channel <strong>11</strong> – (Tone on lock):<br/><em>Set value to<strong> 1</strong></em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><strong>Line 1 <em>(BEFORE the end of 2009)</em>:</strong> <br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 07</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2</strong><em><strong> (If the adaptation channel is not activated</strong>)</em> <strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>10 </strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2: </strong> Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Tick “Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control” (confirmation with Beep/Horn)</em></p>","scirocco-13-door-unlocking-confirmation-key":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Enables door unlocking confirmation to be set when the key is used (for Scirocco before the end of 2009).   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 08</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte<strong> 10</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0: </strong> Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Tick “Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks” (confirmation with beep/horn)</em></p>","scirocco-13-electronic-differential-lock-xds":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the electronic differential lock (XDS).  </p>\n<p>The electronic differential lock (XDS) is an extension of the well-known EDS function. However, XDS does not react to acceleration slip, but rather relieves pressure on the inside front wheel when cornering. XDS applies pressure to the inside wheel during cornering from the hydraulic ESP to prevent slippage.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><em>Byte 17 : </em><br/><em>Bit 3: Tick “(Extended) Electronic Differential Lock (XDS – PR-UG3/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 XDS setting.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10 </strong>”.  </p>\n<p>Channel 36 (Electronic Differential Lock (XDS) in drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value</em><br/> 0<em>“medium” </em><br/>1 “low” <br/>2 “high  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/xdsg6-567d8998.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-activate-driving-school-mode-rcd-210-rcd-310":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Adds a “Driving School” mode view to the RCD 210 / RCD 310 or the Discover MIB2 PQ, which displays turn signals, speed, and more… (Also ideal for accompanied driving) <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h4>RCD 210 / RCD 310</h4>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Channel 2</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>1</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/golf6_golf_vi_fahrschulfunktion-5b883ac1.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<h4>Discover MIB2 PQ:</h4>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule function list CAN-Driving_school</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_driving_school</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_driving_school_over_threshold_high</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6384-e21a59b4.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-enable-usb-port-for-iphone-carplay-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the USB port for iPhone CarPlay accounting (after activating App Connect and changing the USB and/or USB cable) for Discover MIB2 PQ (after 2015). (Retrofit)  </p>\n<p>For firmware references: <br/>MST2_EU_VW_PQ_P02XXT</p>\n<p>Modify MIB2 coding and adaptation to recognize the new USB port (USB connector ref 5Q0 035 726 E) for both CarPlay and USB multimedia playback. A coding device is to be modified on the connector. </p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/app-connect-carplay-activation\">–&gt; App Connect Activation for CarPlay and Android Auto</a><br/><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">–&gt; USB/AUX Port for VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E on VAG Custom</a></strong><br/><a href=\"#/vw/scirocco-13/scirocco-13-deactivate-mirrorlink\"><strong>–&gt; Disable MirrorLink</strong></a><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Assistant Codage Long</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5 </strong>– Select byte<strong>“19</strong>“<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“6-7</strong>” (C0 USB Configuration: USB and iPhone Functionality)<br/><br/><strong>Line 2 (optional) :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong><strong>Interface for external media activation – connection 1</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value “<strong><strong>activated</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><br/></p>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/activation-app-connect-pour-volkswagen/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activation APP CONNECT pour Volkswagen</a></blockquote>\n</figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Prise USB / AUX VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E</a></blockquote>\n</figure>","scirocco-13-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Brake Light active” (to activate brake lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Turn Signal active” (to activate turn signals)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/emergencybreakg6-7e26fa37.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-fog-lamps-with-high-beam":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Prevents the fog lights from turning off when the high beams are on; they will not turn off when you turn on your high beams. (Post-2010)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte<strong> 14</strong>: Clear Bit <strong>2</strong><em> </em>: “<em>Fog lights inactive while high beams are on</em>“</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/antibrouillardpleinphareg6-b0c5522b.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-fold-down-mirrors-with-ignition-off-and-door-open":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Allows mirrors to be folded down even after the ignition has been switched off and a door opened.  </p>\n<p><em>(Also enables windows and sunroof to be closed)</em> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><em>Byte 6 : </em><br/><em>Bit 7: Uncheck “Power Windows/Sunroof disabled after door Opening”.</em></p>","scirocco-13-headlight-washer-duration-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to set how long the headlight washers remain activated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 04</strong> (Headlight Washer Activation Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select a duration between <strong>50 and 10,000 ms</strong> (in 50-ms increments).</p>","scirocco-13-hill-hold-control":"<p><strong>Purpose: Enables </strong>Hill Hold Control (Hill Start Assist).  </p>\n<p>Hill Hold Control maintains brake pressure for a few seconds after the brake pedal is held down for an extended period.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>“</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Hill Hold Control (HHC/PR-UG1/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: Hill Hold Control Settings.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p>Select <strong>Channel 58</strong> (Hill Hold Control (HHC) from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Select a value:<br/>0 “normal”<br/>1 “earlier” (restarts with lower acceleration)<br/>2 “later” (restarts with higher acceleration)</p>","scirocco-13-leaving-home-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is unlocked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 02</strong> (Leaving-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>","scirocco-13-lock-the-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-the-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the RNS 510’s CD/DVD eject button.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 43</strong> (Ejection Lock)</em> then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>(CD/DVD Ejection Lock active)</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-lowering-the-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>09 – Centrale Elec</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf61-d4a12d4d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf62-a22a3a65.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte<strong> 4</strong> and check bit <strong>3 “</strong> <strong>Mirror Lowering With Reverse Rear </strong>” to activate mirror lowering when shifting into reverse gear:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf63-d65eea5e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– After this operation, click on the “Output” menu, then validate “OK”.  </p>\n<p>A message appears to inform you that the coding has been accepted.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:  </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on<strong> “Select” </strong>, then click on<strong> “52 – Passenger door”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Add <strong>256</strong> to the value</em></p>","scirocco-13-mute-push-to-talk-button":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to reconfigure the Push-To-Talk (PTT) button at the bottom left of your multifunction steering wheel to function as a mute button for the audio volume. (2010 and later)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>16 – Multifunction Steering Wheel.”</strong><br/></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding- 07</strong>”. then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 1</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck </em><em>“Multi-Function-Steering-Wheel (MFSW) with Push-To-Talk (PPT) Button installed</em>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/pttg6-da3300eb.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>The Push-to-Talk (PPT) button now acts as a mute button.</p>","scirocco-13-needle-check":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the scanning of the speedometer needles when the car is started. When you start your Scirocco, the needles on the speedometer move back and forth from minimum to maximum. Scirocco R style (from late 2009) (Needle Sweep)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.  </p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>” then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu to choose a channel and select the “<strong>Staging</strong>” channel, if unavailable select the “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” channel:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg6-9456b738.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the “<strong>New value</strong>” box, click on the drop-down menu and select “<strong>active</strong>”. Once this new value has been entered, click on “<strong>Save</strong>”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg62-c8918051.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-odb-color-versions":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to select the version of your color ODB.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/>4 – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>” .<br/><br/>5 – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Display depiction</strong>”.<br/><br/>6 – On this same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, <em>choose “Version 1, Version 2 or Version 3” </em>then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/odb_couleur_193-1cd1bd22.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-oil-temperature-on-the-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the Oil Temperature Display in your Grand ODB.  </p>\n<p>It sometimes happens that certain cars don’t have this value available in the ODB, including certain Sciroccos, TDIs and TSIs, and even R versions. Here’s a short tutorial to help you activate it and make it available in your ODB.  </p>\n<p><em>ATTENTION: Modification cannot be activated on all counters.</em></p>\n<p><br/><em>Information: </em>If the oil temperature gauge on the dashboard is not working, activate the oil on the display to activate it.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/A314693B-5D3C-409F-9FB3-F43FB9417AC6-1024x389-79d7046e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>”, then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu and select this byte: <strong><em>(7) WIV : Service interval coding Oil level and temperature transmitter</em></strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com_01_Sonde_Temperature-d-huile-Golf6R-TSI-TD-913f0cb0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>English version: Coding For Service Interval Extension</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com_01_Sonde_Temperature-d-huile-Golf6R-TSI-TD-6650dcd4.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> <em>Select ”  <strong>Oil level/temp. transmitter connected to instrument holder   </strong>“in the second drop-down list</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1Z0-920-843-G_Module17_Adaptation_7-WIV_v2-73e7e7f3.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_temp_huile_odb-b53aaa02.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-ops-speed-camera-display-on-car-radio-screen":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the display of OPS speed cameras on the car radio screen.  </p>\n<p><strong><em>Please note: The vehicle must be equipped with a compatible car radio (RCD-310, RCD-510, RNS-315, RNS-510).</em></strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“10-Station assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding- 07</strong>”. then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Tick “Optical illustration active”.</em></p>","scirocco-13-permanent-headlight-deactivation-scandinavian":"<p><strong>Purpose: Allows you </strong>to disable the low beams that are always on; they are activated only when set to “Auto,” and during the day, only the parking lights are on. (Disable Scandinavian Mode)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>2008 à 2011:</em></p>\n<p>Uncheck Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>3</strong></p>\n<p><em>From 2011:</em></p>\n<p>Byte <strong>11</strong> Bit <strong>2</strong>: Uncheck “Permanent Running Light (via Low Beam) active”.  </p>","scirocco-13-programming-a-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to program the remote controls that will be used with the vehicle for central locking and unlocking.  </p>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING:</strong> This procedure does not allow you to program remote controls with the vehicle’s immobilizer.<br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Ignition Authorization)</strong>, you cannot program a new remote control using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click <strong>“46 – Comfort Module”</strong>(before the end of 2009) or “ <strong><strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong></strong>” (after the end of 2009).<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01 ( </strong>“Remote Control Adaptation” from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Enter the number of keys to program, then click <strong>Save</strong>.<br/>Next, press the <strong>Unlock</strong> button on each remote control to be programmed for at least 1 second. The flashing lights will confirm the process.<br/>All keys must be programmed in a single session, one after the other.<br/>Programming all keys must not take longer than <strong>15 seconds</strong>.<br/>You can add up to <strong>7 remote controls</strong>. If the <strong>[Test]</strong> and/or <strong>[Save]</strong> buttons are grayed out and unclickable, the module likely has all 7 slots filled; delete the remote controls using the <strong>“Reset Remote Controls”</strong> tutorial.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/programmertelecommande-51bf4068.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-radar-deactivation-speed-or-rearview-camera":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Selects the speed at which the reversing camera and radars are deactivated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“10 – Assistance Stationnt</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Channel 23 ( Choose the new speed, 20 km/h being the maximum )</p>","scirocco-13-make-up-quantity-displayed-on-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the amount of fuel needed to completely fill your tank on the OBD (On-Board Computer). <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10” </strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>“Volume to be Replenished” </strong>from the value list.</p>\n<p>Select ” <strong>Yes</strong> ” in the second value list.</p>","scirocco-13-reset-the-remote-controls":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Resets the settings for all remote controls associated with the vehicle. </p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ WARNING:</strong> After completing this procedure, all remote controls will be deleted and will need to be reprogrammed using the <strong>“Program a Remote Control”</strong> tutorial <strong>.</strong><br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Start Authorization)</strong>, you cannot delete the remote controls using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click <strong>“46 – Comfort Module”</strong>(before the end of 2009) or “ <strong><strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong></strong>” (after the end of 2009).<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 00</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>0</strong> and save</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel00-caced031.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-selective-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Used to set up selective door unlocking. </p>\n<p>When unlocking the vehicle, only the driver’s door is unlocked. To unlock all doors, press the remote control’s unlock button twice.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong><strong>Line 1 <em><strong><em>(AFTER the end of 2009)</em></strong></em> :</strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 3: </strong> Check “Selective Central Locking active (Single Door Locking)” </em> </p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1 <em>(BEFORE the end of 2009)</em></strong><em>: </em><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>46 – Comfort Module.”</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click “ <strong>Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2</strong><em><strong> (If the adaptation channel is not activated</strong>)<strong>:</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0 : </strong> Check “Selective Central Locking (Single Door Opening)”. </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-show-hidden-menu-climatronic":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to display the Climatronic’s hidden menu.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/menu-cache-climatronic-golf5-7154b4a2.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Displaying instantaneous digital speed? it’s possible! </strong>  No need to use your VCDS VAG-COM cable for this tutorial.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong></p>\n<p>It’s really quite simple. <strong>Just press the “ECON” button on your air conditioner and the “air extraction up” button, symbolized by a person with an arrow pointing upwards, at the same time</strong>.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/climatronic1-5edb6af4.gif\"/></figure>\n<p>Then simply move the driver-side climate control knob to access the various temperatures and functions.</p>\n<p><strong>What’s it for?</strong></p>\n<p>The main things to check are engine temperature, cabin temperature, exterior temperature and digital speed.</p>\n<p>For digital speed:  </p>\n<p>Then set to -19.0 in the left-hand display by turning the left-hand knob, and the right-hand display gives you the “real” speed in km/h.</p>\n<p>This is because the “real” speedometer is different from the analogue speedometer (needle) which has passed 60km/h.</p>\n<p>Above 99km/h, the right display alternates between the 100km/h in the small right-hand corner and the remaining two digits in the large right-hand corner.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/climatronic2-1d05bbc0.gif\"/></figure>\n<p>Turning the central knob changes the small exponent number on the left display, which changes the display on the right to a small 2 – the speed is in mph.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/climatronic3-04295505.gif\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>List of hidden Climatronic functions</strong></p>\n<p><br/>The beginning of each paragraph symbolizes a function (1st line) followed by sub-functions (following lines).</p>\n<p><strong>0</strong> System data (temperature setting left)<br/>0 Program number Dig. (temperature setting right)<br/>1 ERL disaster Dig.<br/>2 ERL right Dig.<br/>3 Working point on/on Dig.<br/>4 Automatic ricircolo (motor)/Automatic ricircolo Bit Dig.<br/>5 Heating as stopped I activate Dig.<br/>6 Air quality<br/>7 Derivative Dig.<br/>8 Country code Dig.<br/>9 Zone sensor test °C </p>\n<p><strong>1</strong> UIF (temperature setting left)<br/>0 Internal temperature °C (temperature setting right)<br/>1 Surface temperature °C<br/>2 Platinum piastrin temperature (?) °C<br/>3 Platinum piastrin corrector (?) °C<br/>4 uif-Sonnenint (?) Dig.<br/>5 Radiation corrector (?) °C<br/>6 Dynamic correctors °C<br/>7 Ricircolo corrector °C<br/>8 Thermal correctors °C<br/>9 UIF ignition compensation °C</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> Irradiance sensor SX<br/>0 Irradiance not delayed (?) W/m2<br/>1 Irradiance corrector for temperature controller W/m2<br/>2 Irradiance corrector for fan W/m2<br/>3 Value to be digitized.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> Irradiance sensor DX<br/>0 Irradiance not delayed (?) W/m2<br/>1 Irradiance correction for temperature controller W/m2<br/>2 Irradiance correction for fan W/m2<br/>3 Value to be digitized.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> Outdoor temperature<br/>0 Outdoor temperature °C<br/>1 Temp. Outdoor CAN line °C<br/>2 Intake air temperature climate °C </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> Theoretical SX temperature<br/>0 Theoretical SX outlet air temp. °C<br/>1 Difference between theoretical and actual temp. °C<br/>2 Value of sx. regulation ½ % /Dig<br/>3 Stell-Max (?) ½ % /Dig<br/>4 Defrost SX    </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> Noticed temperature SX<br/>0 Temp. Noticed SX °C<br/>1 Temp. Feet SX °C<br/>2 Temp. Frontal SX °C   </p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> Theoretical temperature DX<br/>0 Theoretical air temperature DX °C<br/>1 Difference between theoretical and actual temperature DX °C<br/>2 Control values controller ½ % /Dig<br/>3 Stell-Max (?) ½ % /Dig<br/>4 Defrost DX   </p>\n<p><strong>8</strong> Noticed temperature DX<br/>0 Noticed outlet air temp. DX °C<br/>1 Temp. Feet °C<br/>2 Temp. Frontal °C   </p>\n<p><strong>9</strong> Theoretical evaporator temperature<br/>0 Theoretical evaporator temperature °C<br/>1 Difference between theoretical and effective evaporator temp. °C<br/>2 Evaporator control values 5mA/Dig<br/>3 Evaporator control modes (see below)  </p>\n<p><strong>10</strong> Effective evaporator temperature<br/>0 Effective evaporator temperature °C<br/>1 Refrigerant pressure climate bar<br/>2 Average refrigerant temperature climate °C</p>\n<p><strong>11</strong> Compressore clim<br/>0 Theoretical electric power but<br/>1 Effective electric power but<br/>2 Max electric power but<br/>3 Kompressor PWM (0… 200) Dig<br/>4 Electric power compressore offset<br/>5 Electric power values<br/>6 Code compressore disinserito</p>\n<p><strong>12</strong> Fan climate<br/>0 Theoretical fan voltage V<br/>1 Manual control<br/>2 Fault code<br/>3 Riduction fan V<br/>4 Offset fan (from here to automatic mode) 0.1V</p>\n<p><strong>13</strong> Bocchette air temperature SX<br/>0 Theoretical value formattato %<br/>1 Theoretical value actual temp. Bocchette sx. Dig.<br/>2 Conferma el. temp. Bocchette sx. Dig.<br/>3 Limite plus grand temp. Bocchette sx. Dig.<br/>4 Limit min. temp. Bocchette sx. Dig.          </p>\n<p><strong>14</strong> Bocchette air temperature DX<br/>0 Theoretical value formattato %<br/>1 Theoretical value real temp. Bocchette dx Dig.<br/>2 Conferma el. temp. Bocchette dx Dig.<br/>3 Limite plus grand temp. Bocchette dx. Dig.<br/>4 Limit min. temp. Bocchette dx. Dig.        </p>\n<p><strong>15</strong> Temperature bocchetta pieds/centrale<br/>0 Theoretical value formattato %<br/>1 Actual theoretical value temp. Bocchetta centrale Dig.<br/>2 Conferma el. temp. bocchetta centrale Dig.<br/>3 Limite plus grand temp. bocchetta centrale Dig.<br/>4 Limite min. temp. bocchetta centrale Dig.      </p>\n<p><strong>16</strong> Pelle Defrost<br/>0 Theoretical value formattato %<br/>1 Actual theoretical value pelle Defrost Dig.<br/>2 Conferma el. pelle Defrost Dig.<br/>3 Limit plus pelle Defrost Dig.<br/>4 Limit min. pelle Defrost Dig.  </p>\n<p><strong>17</strong> Pelle ricircolo interne<br/>0 Valeur théorique formattato %<br/>1 Valeur théorique réelle pelle ricircolo Dig.<br/>2 Conferma el. pelle ricircolo Dig.<br/>3 Limite plus grand pelle ricircolo Dig.<br/>4 Limite min. pelle ricircolo Dig.  </p>\n<p><strong>18</strong> Cold air shovel<br/>0 Theoretical value formattato %<br/>1 Theoretical actual value Cold air shovel Dig.<br/>2 Conferma el. Pelle air froid Dig.<br/>3 Limite plus grand Pelle air froid Dig.<br/>4 Limite min. Cold air shovel Dig.  </p>\n<p><strong>19</strong> Motor data<br/>0 Speeds’ km/h<br/>1 Motor temperature °C<br/>2 Motor rpm U/min<br/>3 Compressor rpm climate U/min</p>\n<p><strong>20</strong> Data sent on CAN<br/>0 of Additional heating (on demand)1 = inserted<br/>1 Conferma el. PTC 1 = inserted<br/>2 Puissance el. effective PTC à 3% air demandé radiatore de<br/>clima%<br/>4 Rappo% de pic de l’air radiatore%<br/>5 Aucune prestation demandée au disp. de chauffage 1=nessuna prestation chauffage   </p>\n<p><strong>21</strong> Ripartitore d’air Climat<br/>0 Defrost% 1 Frontale%<br/>2 Piedi%<br/>3 Bocchetta areazione%<br/>4 Ricircolo air frais/propre (+ bocchetta… ?) %<br/>5 Évaluation sensore%</p>\n<p><strong>22</strong> Timer data<br/>0 Stop period min.<br/>1 Motor running time S<br/>2 Running time with key inserted s</p>\n<p><strong>23</strong> Special channel<br/>0 Internal lighting sensor Dig.<br/>1 Air quality sensor</p>\n<p><strong>24</strong> Software version<br/>0 Development status<br/>1 Software version<br/>2 Type SW<br/>3 Keep Frozen<br/>4 Version K Matrix<br/>5 EEP -Testflags<br/>6 Codifica Vag (?) 2</p>\n<p><strong>25</strong> Canali di prova<br/>0 Canale 0<br/>1 Canale1<br/>2 Canale2<br/>3 Canale3<br/>4 Canale4<br/>5 Canale5<br/>6 Canale6<br/>7 Canale7<br/>8 Canale8<br/>9 Canale9</p>\n<p><strong>26</strong> Parameters for readings on crystals<br/>0 I delay s<br/>1 Step/udm (?) digit<br/>2 Limit minimo digit<br/>3 Limit max. digit<br/>4 Step/udm on HellaKit (?) 1=ein </p>\n<p><strong>27</strong> Bocchetta areazione directe<br/>0 Theoretical value formattato%<br/>1 Actual theoretical value Bocchetta areazione directe Dig.<br/>2 Conferma el. Bocchetta areazione directe Dig.<br/>3 Limite max. Bocchetta areazione directe Dig.<br/>4 Limite min. Bocchetta areazione directe Dig.   </p>\n<p><strong>28</strong> Umidita<br/>0 Umidita’22#teorica%<br/>1 Umidita’relative to temperature UIF ? %<br/>2 Temp. WSS crystals °C<br/>3 Temperature of condensation °C<br/>4 Melting point temperature difference °C </p>\n<p><strong>29</strong> Raw values himidity<br/>0 Temp. Crystals, corrected °C<br/>1 Temp. Crystal, uncorrected °C<br/>2 Sensor umidità%<br/>3 Sensor temperature °C<br/>4 Condensation point temperature (test measurement) °C<br/>5 Fault code  </p>\n<p><strong>30</strong> Indicated values you himidity<br/>0 Sensor value termofil oDig.<br/>1 Temperatura rif. termofilo Dig.<br/>2 Periodic duration himidity 10-4 sec<br/>3 Temp. Reference himidity Dig.<br/>4 Himidity Rel. on sensore%<br/>5 Sensor temperature himidity °C<br/>6 Crystal temperature (uncorrected) °C   </p>\n<p><strong>What’s in it for me?</strong></p>\n<p>None, unless you like numbers, and the fact that you can see your speed in real time other than with a needle is very nice.</p>\n<p><strong>How do I get out of this menu?</strong></p>\n<p>By switching off the engine or pressing the “AUTO” and “ECON” buttons simultaneously.</p>","scirocco-13-sound-reduction-on-ops-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically lowers speaker volume when OPS is activated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“10-Station assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select <em>Channel<strong> 08</strong> (Audio Volume Lowering): </em><br/><em>Set value to<strong> 0</strong></em> </p>","scirocco-13-speed-limit-display-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to display the speed limit on the RNS 510 navigation screen.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”. Then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong><br/>Activate Bit <strong>2</strong>: Speed Threshold for Destination Input active</p>\n<p>+ use voice command to activate Bit 3: Speed Threshold for Speech Destination Input active</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510speed-9dcbaa67.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-start-stop-deactivation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to disable Start and Stop completely.  </p>\n<p><strong><em>Only compatible with Gateway 7N0! Temperature deactivation method. </em></strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Long Adaptation – 0A”</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Channel<strong>“13</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – In new value, select<strong>“D02000</strong>” (default value = <strong>002000</strong>) then validate.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/gof6startstop-1024x528-699ec970.webp\"/></figure>","scirocco-13-tear-wiping":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the windshield wipers once more after using the windshield washer, in order to remove any remaining water from the windshield.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07”</strong> then <strong>“Long Coding Helper”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>, <br/>Check Bit <strong>3</strong></p>","scirocco-13-activate-daytime-running-lights-with-fog-lamps-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows fog lights to be used as daytime running lights.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1</strong><em><strong> (AFTER late 2009)</strong> </em>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte <strong>14: </strong> </em><br/>Set <em>Bit <strong>1</strong> </em> </p>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><strong>Line 1 <em>(BEFORE the end of 2009)</em></strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte <strong>0: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Lights (North America)”</em></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>3</strong></em>: Uncheck</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/scandinavie_194-c7df4fa8.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7 – </strong> <em>Byte <strong>17</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light with dimmed Low Beam” (or “Daytime Running Light via Fog Lights,” depending on your version of VCDS)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/ab_975-e7b60077.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/veilleusejour3-c639151f.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>8-</strong> Adjusting the fog light intensity (from 1% to 99%)</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>20</strong>: </em><br/><em>Change the value in the Dec box (the yellow box)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/VagComByte20-adce5646.webp\"/></figure>"};
